--- a/arm64ec/README.md
+++ b/arm64ec/README.md
@@ -66,6 +66,36 @@ particular the motion-vector sign/scale convention (`motionVectorScale` in the
 Convert pass) is derived rather than measured, and is the first thing to check
 if output looks smeared or inverted.
 
+## Arm ASR
+
+Arm Accuracy Super Resolution (MIT, `LICENSES/MIT-Arm-ASR.txt`; it carries
+AMD's FSR2 copyright too) is AMD's FSR 2.2.2 reworked for mobile GPUs: fp16
+throughout, most passes as full-screen fragment shaders, and a shader quality
+preset independent of the upscaling ratio. Select it with `Dx12Upscaler=asr`
+(or `Dx11Upscaler=asr_12` for the DX11 bridge) and pick the preset with
+`[ASR] ShaderQuality=quality|balanced|performance` (default balanced).
+
+Arm only ships a Vulkan backend, so the pieces here are:
+
+- `build.sh` clones the library at tag 25.06
+  (`0501f490bd9946a2e1806b5363d7ab8a9a6a5e0a`) into `$DEPS/asr` and builds its
+  host library (`ffxmFsr2*`) as `libasr_arm64ec.a`. Its Vulkan backend and
+  prebuilt SPIR-V are not used.
+- `gen_asr_shaders.py` compiles ASR's own HLSL to DXIL (SM6.0, `min16float`)
+  with a Linux DXC into `$DEPS/asrgen/asr_dx12_shaders.h`, together with the
+  binding reflection the backend needs. Permutations whose preprocessed source
+  is identical are compiled once (240 -> 100 blobs, ~0.9 MiB). `build.sh` runs
+  it when that header is missing and `$DXC` (default `dxc`) passes a probe
+  compile; otherwise the DLL builds without ASR and `asr` falls back.
+  Arch's `directx-shader-compiler` 1.10.2605.37-1 (x86_64 and ALARM aarch64)
+  currently aborts on every input; Microsoft's Linux release build works.
+- `OptiScaler/upscalers/asr/ffxm_dx12.cpp` is a D3D12 implementation of ASR's
+  `FfxmInterface` (root signatures from the reflection, graphics PSOs per
+  render-target format set, resource state tracking), and `ASRFeature_Dx12`
+  the OptiScaler feature on top of it. Sharpening uses OptiScaler's RCAS, as
+  for SGSR2, so ASR's own RCAS / sharpened-accumulate / reactive-mask passes
+  are not compiled.
+
 ## Standard defines
 
 ```
